# Fernpage MCP tool catalog

`docs/brief.md` is the source of truth for owner decisions; this document proposes the agent interface and labels the choices made where the brief is silent. This is a design contract, not an implemented MCP server.

## Design

Use familiar file operations for site source, site settings, and saved entries. Saved data stays in the reactive database: its JSON files are an authorized virtual view, not exported copies that must be synced back. Each virtual saved-data file represents exactly one entry. This keeps a small correction small and lets visitors continue writing other entries while an agent works.

Advertise one static catalog of eleven tools. Authorization happens on every call, through the same product capabilities used by the browser app and runtime SDK. No SQL, arbitrary backend execution, upload-staging tools, confirmation flags, or separate publish step is needed.

## Addressing and file view

Every site operation takes the stable `site_id`; creation takes an explicit `workspace_id`. Names and titles are display values, never mutation addresses. IDs are opaque, case-sensitive strings returned by discovery; agents must not construct them. Public URLs are returned by the service rather than assembled by agents.

Paths are absolute within the following **virtual site root**, not the agent's local filesystem:

| Path | Meaning | Publicly served? |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `/files/index.html` | Site entry point | Yes, as `/index.html` and the site root |
| `/files/styles.css`, `/files/assets/logo.png` | Site text and binary assets | Yes, without the `/files` prefix |
| `/settings.json` | Site configuration, including visitor saved-data rules | No |
| `/data/checklist/bring-cake.json` | One saved entry: collection `checklist`, key `bring-cake` | Only through the runtime SDK and its access rules |
| `/data/rsvps/7qKp9Vm2.json` | One RSVP entry; key returned by SDK or discovery | Only through the runtime SDK and its access rules |

`/files`, `/data`, and collection directories are listing prefixes, not writable files. Creating an entry requires its collection to be declared in settings. Removing a collection rule does not delete entries. Saved-data paths are never a static HTTP route; a static file named `data.json` has no special powers.

Require canonical, case-sensitive paths: no `.` or `..` segments, repeated separators, backslashes, encoded separators, NULs, wildcards, or trailing slash on a file path. Validate the decoded address once and reject aliases rather than silently normalizing them. Collection names and entry keys use `[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,64}`; `.json` is the virtual suffix, not part of the key. Keys stay stable when values change and must not contain visitor names or email addresses. Site asset paths may have nested directories and ordinary filename characters under `/files/`.

## Argument schemas

The following JSON Schema bundle defines every tool's `inputSchema`: use `#/$defs/<tool_name>` as its root and resolve shared references within this bundle. All objects reject unknown properties. Byte limits and cross-field/path constraints described below are enforced in addition to schema validation. Optional fields never change the scope of a destructive operation.

```json
